ening yes it appears to  be happening  deaths hit an average peak of about 3  400 deaths per day around the middle of  january  more than a 911 every single day  the trend line sort of plateaued and it  has started to come down  and hopefully will start to come down  more  quickly as people are vaccinated  particularly  folks at highest risk of death so that  gets us to  variance and to get to variants we have  to go through  vaccines currently there are two  vaccines  approved for emergency use in the united  states  first was the pfizer vaccine then the  moderna vaccine  early concerns about  supply and delivery have been replaced  by  more cautious optimism from pfizer and  moderna about their ability to continue  delivering millions of doses per day  as many of you know i was on a sort of  on-call list for leftover doses at the  end of the day a friend of mine works at  a hospital that has a  zero waste commitment on doses and  i was able to get my first dose of the  moderna vaccine about 10 days ago from a  left overdose  from cancelled appointments and the  numbers continue to improve the u.s is  now giving out  an average of 1.46 million doses per day  remember joe biden's goal  was 1 million doses per day for 100 days  we're at 1.46 million doses per day and  on saturday and sunday the us  actually did 2 million doses each day  2 million on saturday 2 million on  sunday that is  absolutely fantastic if we get a third  vaccine approved in the next three weeks  johnson johnson has submitted their  vaccine for approval that's a one-dose  vaccine not inconceivable that the u.s  could get to  2.5 million doses per day  i mean i want to be careful but even 3  million doses per day  which would be absolutely fantastic and  the one dose nature of the jnj vaccine  makes the legit the logistics even  easier  now case is down death's starting to  come down  vaccination's starting to go up what  about  the covet variants there is a lot of  doom and gloom about the covet